Dear All,

Unfortunately, I have problems combining full matching and exact matching. I want to do exact matching on the cluster variable „IDA“, and full matching on all other variables. The propensity score I calculated previously is called „PS“ and I use it as distance measure. The dataset is called "impute1“. The treatment variable is "teilgenommen“ and it is predicted by many covariates (e.g., t1_age + STLT1nmath + STLT1ndeu).

In the documentation of the package I read that for nearest neighbor matching it is very simple to combine nearest neighbor and exact matching. I tried to use this approach for full matching  but it did not work. I am not very good in writing complex functions or even understanding very complex functions.

If anybody can give me some advice I appreciate it.

I tried the following:

First:
test <- matchit (teilgenommen ~ t1_age + STLT1nmath + STLT1ndeu +   
                     sgeschlecht + s1kt01flu +
                     hisei +  
                     Zgc + Zgf + 
                     s1int_deu + s1int_mat + 
                     s1int_mnk + s1int_spr + 
                     s1ria_i + s1ria_r + s1ria_a + 
